{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a queue, an urgency, and a yes or no from a ticket that stays on your machine.\nInstall Ollaya.\nThen pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollayaDecider"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter covers evaluate only.\nIt sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"POST /v1/systemone"},{"type":"text","value":" to a local Ollaya server with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThere is no Ollaya SDK."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS or Linux, run:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"curl -fsSL https://ollaya.dev/install.sh | sh","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows, run this in PowerShell:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"irm https://ollaya.dev/install.ps1 | iex","lang":"powershell"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server listens on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://127.0.0.1:11435"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThis adapter uses that URL by default."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollaya serve"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollaya pull laya:latest"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The download page and the desktop app are on "},{"type":"link","href":"https://ollaya.dev/download","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ollaya.dev/download"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install-the-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the adapter"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value);\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value);\nconsole.log(result.refund.value);\nconsole.log(result.meta.model);\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You now have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.queue.value"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.urgency.value"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.refund.value"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../evaluate/evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the rest of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you request "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:latest"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.meta.model"},{"type":"text","value":" can be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:en"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:multilingual"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe server picks the model from the text."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:latest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Routes each request to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:en"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:multilingual"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:en"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"English decision model (ModernBERT-large)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya:multilingual"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decision model for 100+ languages (mmBERT-base)."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can pass any other model tag as a string."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"host-and-api-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host and API key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default the adapter calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://127.0.0.1:11435"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe adapter does not read environment variables.\nIf the server is on another host, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":".\nIf the server requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OLLAYA_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":", pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst adapter = ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\", {\n  baseURL: \"http://my-host:11435\",\n  apiKey: \"local-token\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" are aliases of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":".\nIf you set both forms, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" win.\nA blank "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the default host."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ollayadecider-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollayaDecider(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an evaluate adapter."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"laya:latest\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"laya:en\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"laya:multilingual\""},{"type":"text","value":", or another model tag"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":": server URL (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://127.0.0.1:11435"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias. A blank value keeps the default."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":": bearer token when the server requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OLLAYA_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":": extra request headers. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.fetch"},{"type":"text","value":": override "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"POST /v1/systemone"},{"type":"text","value":" to that base URL."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../evaluate/evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":": full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" walkthrough"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate a ticket"}]},{"type":"text","value":": build a Start route"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"install-the-server","text":"Install the server","level":2},{"id":"install-the-adapter","text":"Install the adapter","level":2},{"id":"evaluate","text":"Evaluate","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"host-and-api-key","text":"Host and API key","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API reference","level":2},{"id":"ollayadecider-model-config","text":"ollayaDecider(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a queue, an urgency, and a yes or no from a ticket that stays on your machine.\nInstall Ollaya.\nThen pass `ollayaDecider` to `decide()`.\n\nThe adapter covers evaluate only.\nIt sends `POST /v1/systemone` to a local Ollaya server with `fetch`.\nThere is no Ollaya SDK.\n\n## Install the server\n\nOn macOS or Linux, run:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://ollaya.dev/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nOn Windows, run this in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nirm https://ollaya.dev/install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\nThe server listens on `http://127.0.0.1:11435`.\nThis adapter uses that URL by default.\n\n1. Run `ollaya serve`.\n2. Run `ollaya pull laya:latest`.\n\nThe download page and the desktop app are on [ollaya.dev/download](https://ollaya.dev/download).\n\n## Install the adapter\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Evaluate\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value);\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value);\nconsole.log(result.refund.value);\nconsole.log(result.meta.model);\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);\n```\n\nYou now have `result.queue.value`, `result.urgency.value`, and `result.refund.value`.\n\nSee [Evaluate](../evaluate/evaluate) for the rest of `decide()`.\n\nWhen you request `laya:latest`, `result.meta.model` can be `laya:en` or `laya:multilingual`.\nThe server picks the model from the text.\n\n## Models\n\n| Model               | Description                                              |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `laya:latest`       | Routes each request to `laya:en` or `laya:multilingual`. |\n| `laya:en`           | English decision model (ModernBERT-large).               |\n| `laya:multilingual` | Decision model for 100+ languages (mmBERT-base).         |\n\nYou can pass any other model tag as a string.\n\n## Host and API key\n\nBy default the adapter calls `http://127.0.0.1:11435`.\nThe adapter does not read environment variables.\nIf the server is on another host, pass `baseURL`.\nIf the server requires `OLLAYA_API_KEY`, pass `apiKey`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst adapter = ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\", {\n  baseURL: \"http://my-host:11435\",\n  apiKey: \"local-token\",\n});\n```\n\n`baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`.\nIf you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\nA blank `baseURL` keeps the default host.\n\n## API reference\n\n### `ollayaDecider(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an evaluate adapter.\n\n- `model`: `\"laya:latest\"`, `\"laya:en\"`, `\"laya:multilingual\"`, or another model tag\n- `config.baseURL`: server URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:11435`). `baseUrl` is an alias. A blank value keeps the default.\n- `config.apiKey`: bearer token when the server requires `OLLAYA_API_KEY`\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n- `config.fetch`: override `fetch`\n\nThe adapter sends `POST /v1/systemone` to that base URL.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Evaluate guide](../evaluate/evaluate): full `decide()` walkthrough\n- [Evaluate a ticket](../tutorials/evaluate): build a Start route\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Ollaya\nid: ollaya-adapter\ndescription: \"Call decide() on a local Ollaya server with @tanstack/ai-ollaya.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - ollaya\n  - laya\n  - evaluate\n  - decide\n  - typed decisions\n  - adapter\n---\n\nYou want a queue, an urgency, and a yes or no from a ticket that stays on your machine.\nInstall Ollaya.\nThen pass `ollayaDecider` to `decide()`.\n\nThe adapter covers evaluate only.\nIt sends `POST /v1/systemone` to a local Ollaya server with `fetch`.\nThere is no Ollaya SDK.\n\n## Install the server\n\nOn macOS or Linux, run:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://ollaya.dev/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nOn Windows, run this in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nirm https://ollaya.dev/install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\nThe server listens on `http://127.0.0.1:11435`.\nThis adapter uses that URL by default.\n\n1. Run `ollaya serve`.\n2. Run `ollaya pull laya:latest`.\n\nThe download page and the desktop app are on [ollaya.dev/download](https://ollaya.dev/download).\n\n## Install the adapter\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-ollaya\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Evaluate\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value);\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value);\nconsole.log(result.refund.value);\nconsole.log(result.meta.model);\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);\n```\n\nYou now have `result.queue.value`, `result.urgency.value`, and `result.refund.value`.\n\nSee [Evaluate](../evaluate/evaluate) for the rest of `decide()`.\n\nWhen you request `laya:latest`, `result.meta.model` can be `laya:en` or `laya:multilingual`.\nThe server picks the model from the text.\n\n## Models\n\n| Model               | Description                                              |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `laya:latest`       | Routes each request to `laya:en` or `laya:multilingual`. |\n| `laya:en`           | English decision model (ModernBERT-large).               |\n| `laya:multilingual` | Decision model for 100+ languages (mmBERT-base).         |\n\nYou can pass any other model tag as a string.\n\n## Host and API key\n\nBy default the adapter calls `http://127.0.0.1:11435`.\nThe adapter does not read environment variables.\nIf the server is on another host, pass `baseURL`.\nIf the server requires `OLLAYA_API_KEY`, pass `apiKey`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { ollayaDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollaya\";\n\nconst adapter = ollayaDecider(\"laya:latest\", {\n  baseURL: \"http://my-host:11435\",\n  apiKey: \"local-token\",\n});\n```\n\n`baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`.\nIf you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\nA blank `baseURL` keeps the default host.\n\n## API reference\n\n### `ollayaDecider(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an evaluate adapter.\n\n- `model`: `\"laya:latest\"`, `\"laya:en\"`, `\"laya:multilingual\"`, or another model tag\n- `config.baseURL`: server URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:11435`). `baseUrl` is an alias. A blank value keeps the default.\n- `config.apiKey`: bearer token when the server requires `OLLAYA_API_KEY`\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n- `config.fetch`: override `fetch`\n\nThe adapter sends `POST /v1/systemone` to that base URL.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Evaluate guide](../evaluate/evaluate): full `decide()` walkthrough\n- [Evaluate a ticket](../tutorials/evaluate): build a Start route\n"}
